# Shared Infra Changelog (perf lane)

This lane makes the backend size workers/threads/DB pools dynamically from a
cgroup-aware detector (`shared/ai_mesh_shared/resource_budget.py`). Changes that
affect the shared stack are mirrored here, in `docs/perf/CHANGELOG.md`,
`AGENTS.md` (## Shared Infra Changes), and Ruflo `shared/infra-changes`.

Newest first.

## PERF-0008 — soc-kpis BRIN index on EnforcementEvent.created_at (2026-07-03) [DB SCHEMA]
- Item 18. Migration `policy/0036_ev_created_at_brin` adds a standalone BRIN index on
  `created_at` (the composite index leads with organization, useless for a
  created_at-only window). Applied CONCURRENTLY (no lock) — **already live on the
  shared DB**. Backward-compatible. AFFECTS: shared Postgres schema. ACTION: `docker
  compose build control` at convenience; migrate then no-ops (0036 already applied);
  no restart. PROOF: index 40kB; selective window → Bitmap Index Scan on
  ev_created_at_brin, 0.3ms. Dominant 24-30s cost is metadata-JSON hauling (items 19-20).

## PERF-0007 — Redis/cache pools sized from the detector (2026-07-03)
- Detector gains `redis_pool = clamp(asgi_threads*4, 64, 256)` (6c=64, 12c=96, 16c=128).
  `gateway/entrypoint.sh` exports `GATEWAY_REDIS_MAX_CONNECTIONS` (middleware pool, was
  300); `control/server-entrypoint.sh` exports `DJANGO_CACHE_MAX_CONNECTIONS` (was 200).
  Generous per-worker lazy ceilings, scale with cores, never bottleneck (Redis 49/10000).
  Gateway hot-path REDIS_CLIENT left unbounded (safe). Vault done in PERF-0005. Explicit
  env overrides. AFFECTS: gateway+control images. ACTION: `docker compose build gateway
  control`; running containers not recreated. PROOF: --cpus=6 → both =64; 20 tests green.

## PERF-0006 — Postgres max_connections=400 confirmed sufficient, NO restart (2026-07-03)
- Item 15. Measured: control ~2.5 DB conns/worker (sync-view serialization), not the
  detector worst-case. `scripts/perf/pg_budget.py` derives the stack recommendation:
  6c→107, 12c→185, 16c→257 — all < the deployed 400 (live usage 16/400). CONN_MAX_AGE=60
  sane. NO docker-compose/Postgres change, NO restart. Worker-count changes
  (PERF-0001/0002) do not risk PG exhaustion on target profiles.
- ACTION: none. For >~24c boxes set POSTGRES_MAX_CONNECTIONS from pg_budget.py (restarts
  PG) or add pgbouncer.

## PERF-0005 — Gateway scanner/bedrock/vault pools sized from detector (2026-07-03)
- Detector gains scanner_pool/bedrock_pool/vault_pool (clamped: scanner clamp(cpu,4,16),
  bedrock=asgi_threads, vault clamp(cpu/2,2,8)). `gateway/entrypoint.sh` exports
  GATEWAY_SCANNER/SCAN_THREAD_POOL_SIZE, GATEWAY_BEDROCK_THREAD_POOL_SIZE,
  GATEWAY_VAULT_POOL_MAX from the detector (was fixed 8/4/16/8). Explicit env overrides.
  Pools clamped because each ×workers (item 11); vault feeds pg (item 15).
- AFFECTS: gateway image (resource_budget.py change is additive). ACTION: `docker compose
  build gateway`. Running container not recreated. PROOF: --cpus=6 → scanner=6, bedrock=12,
  vault=3; scanner logs thread_pool_size=6; override honored; 19 detector tests green.

## PERF-0004 — Control ASGI sync-offload thread pool sized from detector (2026-07-03)
- `control/main_app/asgi.py` sizes the event-loop default thread pool per worker from
  `ASGI_THREADS` (entrypoint exports it from the detector: 6c=12, 12c=24), replacing
  Python's non-cgroup-aware `min(32, os.cpu_count()+4)`. Thread-sensitive Django views
  untouched (P4). `ASGI_THREADS` env overrides. AFFECTS: control image. ACTION:
  `docker compose build control`. Running container not recreated.

## PERF-0003 — Harden gateway+control entrypoints vs empty WEB_CONCURRENCY (2026-07-03)
- Both entrypoints now `export WEB_CONCURRENCY="$WORKERS"` before exec'ing gunicorn —
  gunicorn reads WEB_CONCURRENCY at config-import time and crashes on an empty string
  (`int('')`). AFFECTS: gateway+control images (rebuilt). ACTION: `docker compose build
  gateway control`. No behavior change for valid configs; prevents a boot crash when
  `WEB_CONCURRENCY=` (empty) is in the env. Running containers not recreated.

## PERF-0002 — Control: single Daphne → gunicorn + N UvicornWorker (2026-07-03)
- Control image now runs `gunicorn main_app.asgi:application -k
  uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker --workers N --forwarded-allow-ips *` (N from the
  detector) via `control/server-entrypoint.sh`, replacing the single Daphne (dev) /
  hardcoded `--workers 5` (prod). `CONTROL_WEB_CONCURRENCY` env overrides.
- Multiproc-safe: telemetry drain is per-hostname single-runner-locked; resync/seed
  idempotent. Boot verified: 4 workers serve `/api/health/` 200.
- AFFECTS: `ai_mesh_firewall-control` image. ACTION: `docker compose build control`.
  Running container NOT recreated (shared host still single Daphne). ⚠️ Before
  recreating on the 16-core host, pin `CONTROL_WEB_CONCURRENCY` (e.g. 6) — an
  unpinned recreate = 16 workers and can pressure Postgres `max_connections=400`
  (sized in a later item). Recreate: `docker compose up -d --force-recreate control`.

## PERF-0001 — Gateway WEB_CONCURRENCY derived from the detector (2026-07-03)
- Gateway image now runs `gateway/entrypoint.sh`, which sets gunicorn `--workers`
  from the detector (one UvicornWorker/core, RAM-bounded) instead of the hardcoded
  `${WEB_CONCURRENCY:-4}`. Explicit `WEB_CONCURRENCY` env still overrides.
- AFFECTS: `ai_mesh_firewall-gateway` image. ACTION: `docker compose build gateway`
  to adopt. Behavior UNCHANGED on the shared host (`.env` pins `WEB_CONCURRENCY=6`);
  no DB change, no forced restart. Running container not recreated.
- Proof: `--cpus=6`→6 workers, `--cpus=12`→12 workers, `WEB_CONCURRENCY=3`→3.
